-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
Usage: gccli body export-blood-pressure --start=DATE --end=DATE [flags]

Save the blood pressure report of a date range as PDF or JSON.

Garmin creates the report and the command waits for it, up to two minutes.
Garmin offers PDF and JSON only. An existing output file is overwritten. For the
readings as data, use body blood-pressure.

Flags:
  -h, --help              Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json              Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain             Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header            Print the column names as the first line of --plain
                          output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"      Color mode: auto, always, never ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING    Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"      Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                          elevations and weights in table and plain output:
                          auto (Garmin profile), metric, statute_us, statute_uk
                          ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version           Print version information.

      --start=DATE        Start date (YYYY-MM-DD, today, yesterday, 3d, +30d).
      --end=DATE          End date (YYYY-MM-DD, today, yesterday, 3d, +30d).
      --period=PERIOD     Report layout: daily, seven-days, four-weeks or
                          yearly. Default: the shortest one that covers the
                          range.
      --format="pdf"      File format: pdf or json.
  -o, --output=STRING     Output file path (default:
                          blood_pressure_{start}_{end}.{format}).

